      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While greens are certainly healthy, you need to be mindful of certain leafy greens when taking warfarin. Spinach, for example, contains Vitamin K, which can interfere with how your blood thins. Instead of massive, sudden changes, aim for consistent, moderate servings of various vegetables to keep your Vitamin K intake stable. Be sure to discuss specific amounts with your healthcare provider to keep your INR in the target range.",
